    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276-a2">

                <pb facs="0749" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg627"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of the Chief of Engineers,<lb/>United States
                                Army</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                            C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-12-17"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">December</hi> 17,
                    1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    report, just received, from Major O. H. Ernst, Corps of Engineers, U. S. Army,
                    addressed to the honorable the Secretary of State, in the matter of the works of
                    construction by the Mexican Government for the protection of the right bank of
                    the Rio Grande at El Paso, Texas.</p>
                <p>As the report is made in compliance with instructions from the Department of
                    State (with the sanction of the War Department), it is forwarded at once.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. Lincoln Casey</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Brig. Gen., Chief of Engineers.</hi></item>
                            <item>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William C. Endicott</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Secretary of War.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
